# Retrospective on completed tasks

You are reviewing {{issueCount}} completed Octestra tasks to find recurring friction and improve the
instructions future tasks receive.

## Tasks in scope

{{#each issues}}
- #{{number}} — {{title}} (updated {{updated_at}})
{{/each}}

## What to do

1. For each task, read the issue and the pull request that closed it, including review comments,
   requested changes, and any Blocked transitions.
2. Look for patterns rather than one-off mistakes: instructions that were repeatedly misread,
   acceptance criteria that were repeatedly missed, review comments that recur across tasks.
3. Edit `.github/octestra/prompts/` and the agent skill files so that a future task would avoid
   those patterns. Change instructions, not history: do not edit closed issues or merged pull
   requests.

Leave your edits in the working tree. Do not commit, push, or open a pull request — a separate
trusted job turns your changes into a pull request on `{{branchName}}`, and this job holds no
credentials to do it itself.

## Result document

Write JSON to `{{resultPath}}`:

- `outcome` (required): `passed` when you propose changes, `no_action` when the tasks show no
  recurring problem worth changing.
- `summary` (required): what pattern you found and what you changed, for a reader who has not read
  the tasks.
- `details` (optional): Markdown with the per-task evidence behind the pattern.

Do not set `next_status`. An aggregate loop has no single task to move, so it is ignored.

Save any supporting files under `{{artifactPath}}`.
